drivers/net/igbvf/igbvf.h in 2.6.37-rc5 kernel has

/*
* wrappers around a pointer to a socket buffer,
* so a DMA handle can be stored along with the buffer */ struct igbvf_buffer {
dma_addr_t dma;
struct sk_buff *skb;
union {
/* Tx */
struct {
unsigned long time_stamp;
u16 length;
u16 next_to_watch;
u16 mapped_as_page;
};
/* Rx */
struct {
struct page *page;
u64 page_dma;
unsigned int page_offset;
};
};
struct page *page;
};

There are 2 "page" fields. The older GCC doesn't detect this error and will
generate undefined assembly codes when the page field is accessed.

Routing determination: network. Regression assessment: not a regression.

